    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the value of the expression \\(x^2 + 5x - 6\\) when \\(x = -1\\), we will substitute \\(x = -1\\) into the expression and simplify step by step.\n\n1. Start with the expression:\n   \\[\n   x^2 + 5x - 6\n   \\]\n\n2. Substitute \\(x = -1\\) into the expression:\n   \\[\n   (-1)^2 + 5(-1) - 6\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\((-1)^2\\):\n   \\[\n   (-1)^2 = 1\n   \\]\n   So the expression now is:\n   \\[\n   1 + 5(-1) - 6\n   \\]\n\n4. Calculate \\(5(-1)\\):\n   \\[\n   5(-1) = -5\n   \\]\n   So the expression now is:\n   \\[\n   1 - 5 - 6\n   \\]\n\n5. Perform the addition and subtraction from left to right:\n   \\[\n   1 - 5 = -4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -4 - 6 = -10\n   \\]\n\nSo the value of the expression \\(x^2 + 5x - 6\\) when \\(x = -1\\) is \\(\\boxed{-10}\\).",
